5. Understanding Confusion Matrix
The confusion matrix checks how correctly our model predicts diabetes.
\[
\begin{bmatrix}TN & FP\\FN & TP\end{bmatrix}
\]

Term	Meaning
TN	Correctly predicted No Diabetes
TP	Correctly predicted Diabetes
FP	Predicted Diabetes, but actually No Diabetes
FN	Predicted No Diabetes, but actually Diabetes

6. Important Performance Metrics
1. Accuracy

Percentage of total correct predictions.
\[
Accuracy = \frac{TP+TN}{TP+TN+FP+FN}
\]

2. Error Rate

Percentage of incorrect predictions.
\[
Error = 1 - Accuracy
\]

3. Precision

Out of all predicted diabetes cases, how many were actually diabetic?
\[
Precision = \frac{TP}{TP+FP}
\]

4. Recall

Out of all actual diabetes cases, how many were correctly identified?
\[
Recall = \frac{TP}{TP+FN}
\]

