9. Viva Questions and Answers
Q1. What is KNN?

KNN stands for K-Nearest Neighbors. It predicts a class based on nearby data points.

Q2. What is diabetes prediction?

It predicts whether a person has diabetes based on medical information.

Q3. What is Outcome in diabetes.csv?

Outcome is the target column. 0 means No Diabetes and 1 means Diabetes.

Q4. What is K in KNN?

K represents the number of nearest neighbors considered for prediction.

Q5. Why do we use StandardScaler?

To bring all input features to a similar scale.

Q6. What is a confusion matrix?

It is a table used to evaluate classification predictions.

Q7. What is precision?

Correct positive predictions divided by all positive predictions.

Q8. What is recall?

Correctly identified positive cases divided by all actual positive cases.

Q9. What is error rate?

The percentage of incorrect predictions.

Q10. Why do we use train-test split?

To train the model on one part of the data and test it on unseen data.

